<section class="about-grid section-pad" data-reveal><img src="/images/portrait.svg" alt="Darina Mikityuk in her studio" /><div class="about-copy"><p class="lead">Darina Mikityuk is a visual artist whose work moves between painting, sculpture and spatial installation.</p><p>Rooted in an attentive relationship to material, her practice considers how memory takes physical form. Layers of pigment, textile and found matter become quiet records of touch, time and transformation.</p><p>Born in Ukraine and currently based in Berlin, Darina has presented her work through exhibitions, artist-led projects and interdisciplinary collaborations across Europe.</p></div><aside><p class="eyebrow">Selected</p><p>2025 · The Space Between<br />Solo exhibition, Berlin</p><p>2024 · Soft Architecture<br />Site-specific project, Kyiv</p><p>2023 · In Plain Air<br />Group exhibition, Vienna</p></aside></section></Layout>
